1:["$","$Le",null,{"record":{"slug":"amend-pingnan","section":"practice","title":["图书馆片段与公共种子","Library Fragments + Civic Seeds"],"date":"日期未注明 / Undated","status":["教学任务书","Teaching brief"],"summary":["THE AMEND PROJECT: PINGNAN。通过在地观察、材料再用与共同制作，探索社区图书馆与小型公共空间的可能。","THE AMEND PROJECT: PINGNAN proposes field observation, reuse and collective making as a route toward a community library and civic spaces."],"chapters":[{"title":["多人共作一座图书馆","One library, many authors"],"text":["任务书要求每组从地方材料、工艺或故事中寻找线索，制作一个图书馆片段，最终共同组成可使用的空间。这是任务安排，不是已建成成果清单。","Each group is asked to develop a library fragment from local materials, techniques or stories. Together they would form one usable place. These are assignments, not verified completed works."]},{"title":["发现社区需求","Finding a civic need"],"text":["另一条任务从村庄的真实需要出发，提出公共空间“种子”，在杭州汇报并进一步发展。原文件未注明年份、具体届次或图书馆选址，不默认落位小院。","A parallel task asks groups to identify a civic need, present a seed in Hangzhou and develop it further. The brief does not specify a year, cohort or library site; no courtyard location is assumed."]}],"related":["tea-salt-road","workshop-plan"],"sources":["brief"]}}]
